Package: os7-module
Version: @OS7_VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Bastian Wirth <bastian.wirth@upinblue.com>
Section: admin
Priority: important
Depends: os7-powershell (= @OS7_VERSION@)
Recommends: zfsutils-linux
Homepage: https://github.com/upinblue/os7
Description: The OS/7 PowerShell modules and the five layers beneath them
 OS/7's own command surface: the release identity, storage, boot environments,
 rollback, updates, backup, home directories, the network, the clock, services
 and Active Directory, as PowerShell cmdlets — and the five generic layers they
 run on.
 .
 SIX MODULES, and the direction between them is the point. Zfs, Net, Time,
 Systemd and Directory know nothing about OS/7 and would each run on any Ubuntu
 host: ZFS, netplan and iproute2, chrony and the zone files, units and the
 journal, and LDAP with the X.500 and Active Directory schema. OS7 is the
 product layer above all five and reaches every one of those subsystems only
 through them. They travel in one package because that rule is only true if all
 six are present — an OS7 module on a machine missing a layer beneath it is a
 module whose first call to that subsystem throws, naming a module the operator
 never asked for.
 .
 zfsutils-linux is a Recommends and not a Depends on purpose: the modules load,
 report and self-test on a machine with no pools, which is what makes them
 checkable during an image build and on a rescue system.
